      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The main understandability issue is that all test arguments are crammed onto a single line with a `// @formatter:off` guard. I'll reformat the data provider with one case per line and add comments explaining what each boundary represents.Now I'll compile-check it.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version formats each test case on its own line with inline comments explaining the boundary semantics (exact lower/upper bounds of 32-bit Unix time, just-outside-bounds cases, and far-future case), and removes the `// @formatter:off` guard that was only needed to suppress warnings about the dense single-line original."
